# playpick cell: mode=daily spec=priest:shadow style=melee view=1280x800
# save=carried. boss=saved is playpick's own filler for an axis daily does not
# actually expose (direction.md's long-standing note: daily.boss is not
# reachable as a playpick axis) -- confirmed with a `tap daily` + `targets`
# probe before writing this script, same as every prior daily session's
# recipe: today's real daily is The Bonegrinder, 25-player, normal, SWARMING
# (twice as many thralls, half as often).
#
# What is new here: priest:shadow has zero prior readings in sessions.jsonl in
# *any* mode, and mode=daily paired with style=melee has never been run
# either. melee style (scripts/playbot.ts:952) closes to within 4 units of the
# boss and holds there regardless of the spec's own range or melee flag, so a
# cloth caster with melee:false and 900 armor -- squishier than any class
# already tried under this style -- gets dragged into point-blank range of
# whatever the boss's own proximity mechanic is (bonegrinder's bonestorm, the
# subject of open issue #267). carried save is requested by the cell; #273
# (open) means it will behave as fresh regardless -- noted, not re-filed.
open
tap daily
targets
shot daily-screen
tap class:6
shot class-selected
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
state
targets
ui
play melee 200
bill
state
says
shot end
